<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerard of Alsace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1030–1070</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> was Duke of Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> from 1048 to 1070, appointed by Emperor Henry III. He founded the House of Lorraine, whose descendants ruled the duchy until 1737 and, through Francis Stephen, later became the Habsburg-Lorraine dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>.</p></div>
